OL,3,AEswatini gives illegal foreign
OL,4,Abusinesses 12 months to leave
OL,5,
OL,6,FThe legislation follows complaints from
OL,7,Flocal traders that foreign-owned
OL,8,Fbusinesses are encroaching on
OL,9,Ftraditional retail markets, increasing
OL,10,Fcompetition and threatening
OL,11,Flivelihoods.
OL,13,FSouth Africa has witnessed more severe
OL,14,Fenforcement actions, including raids,
OL,15,Farrests and the disruption of
OL,16,Fforeign-run informal businesses, while
OL,17,FKenya has also stepped up action
OL,18,Fagainst foreign traders.
